# ADR-036: Application-Scoped Entity Creation (Strict Hierarchy Enforcement)

## Status
Accepted

## Context
ADR-023 defined Application → Device → Workflow → Dashboard as the platform hierarchy.
ADR-035 added intra-application prerequisites (device before workflow, etc.).
However, global list pages (/devices, /workflows, /dashboards) still allowed creating
entities with no applicationId, producing orphaned records not visible in any Application
Detail page. This violated ADR-023's intent and confused the user setup flow.

## Decision
Entity creation is ONLY permitted within an application context:

**Backend (authoritative)**
- DeviceService.create(): throw 422 if applicationId is missing
- WorkflowService.create(): throw 422 if applicationId is missing (existing device guard retained)
- DashboardService.saveDashboard(): throw 422 if applicationId is missing
  (existing device + workflow guard retained)
- All three controllers: catch prerequisite/scope errors → HTTP 422

**Frontend (UX gate)**
- /devices page: Remove "Add Device" button; show "Add devices from the Application Detail page"
  with a link to /applications
- /workflows page: Remove "Create Workflow" button; same guidance
- /dashboards page: Remove "New Dashboard" button; same guidance
- Application Detail page remains the ONLY creation entry point (already enforced)

## Consequences
- No orphaned entities — every Device, Workflow, Dashboard belongs to an Application
- Enforces ADR-023 hierarchy at both API and UI layers
- Global list pages become read-only browse/manage views
- Users must create an Application before any other entity (existing /applications page handles this)
